2. Introduction:
● This test plan defines the testing strategy, scope, objectives, resources, schedule, and
responsibilities required for testing the Smart Event & Concert Ticket Booking Management
System.
● The system enables users to register and log in, discover events, filter by category or genre, selectseats using an interactive seat map, apply promo codes, make payments through a third-party
payment gateway, and receive digital tickets with QR codes.
● The system also provides an organizer portal for event management and analytics.
● Testing will verify that the system functions correctly, securely, reliably, and efficiently according
to the Software Requirements Specification (SRS).
● The main objective is to ensure correct event discovery, seat availability and locking, booking and payment processing, ticket/QR issuance, organizer functions, data integrity, performance, and
reliability.

3. Test Scope:
In-scope:
● User registration, login, authentication, and profile management
● Event search, discovery, category/genre filtering, and event details
● Interactive seat map, seat selection, temporary seat locking, and booking
● Checkout, order summary, promo code validation, and total calculation
● Payment processing through the integrated payment gateway interface
● Booking confirmation and digital ticket issuance
● QR-code generation and downloadable PDF ticket
● Confirmation email generation through the email service
● Organizer portal, event management, and analytics
● Database storage/retrieval of users, events, seats, bookings, and ticket information
● Performance, security, concurrency, availability, backup/recovery, and usability requirements
Out of scope:
● Physical printing and mailing of tickets
● Manufacturing/testing of physical gate or scanning hardware
● Direct bank ledger auditing
● Internal implementation testing of third-party payment gateway and email-provider infrastructure

4. Test Items:
1. User Authentication & Profile Management – Registration, login, validation, secure password
storage, token handling, and role-based access.
2. Event Search & Discovery – Event search, category/genre filtering, and event information
