6. Level of Testing and Testing Strategies:
6.1 Unit Testing
Individual components such as authentication, event filtering, seat-locking logic, promo-code validation,
payment handling, ticket generation, and database operations will be tested independently. Strategy: use
valid, invalid, boundary, and exception inputs.
6.2 Integration Testing
Interactions will be tested across: User Login → Event Search → Event Selection → Seat Selection →
Seat Lock → Checkout → Payment → Booking Confirmation → QR Ticket/Email. Strategy: verify
correct data and state transfer.
6.3 System Testing
The complete web application will be tested as an integrated system. Strategy: execute complete customer
and organizer workflows.
6.4 Acceptance Testing
The system will be tested against the functional and non-functional requirements and acceptance criteria
defined in the SRS.

7. Testing Types:
7.1 Functional Testing
Verifying each system function produces the expected result for valid and invalid inputs.
7.2 Performance Testing
Verify page-load performance, seat-map response time, and concurrent booking-request handling.
7.3 Security Testing
Verify authentication, authorization, HTTPS, password protection, RBAC, and protection from
unauthorized access.
7.4 Usability Testing
Check ease of navigation through event discovery, seat selection, checkout, payment, and ticket
download.
7.5 Compatibility Testing
Verify operation across supported browsers and common desktop/mobile screen sizes.7.6 Regression Testing
Ensure existing event, booking, payment, and ticket functions continue to work after changes.
7.7 Validation Testing
Verify the final system meets the SRS requirements and acceptance criteria.
7.8 Reliability & Recovery Testing
Verify handling of payment/network failures, seat-lock expiry, backups, and recovery.

