11. Entry Criteria:
Testing will begin when:
● A testable software build is available.
● The test environment is ready and accessible.
● Test cases and test data are prepared and approved.
● The SRS and project documentation are available.
● The major development phase for the tested build is completed.
● Mock payment responses and representative event/seat data are available.
12. Exit Criteria:
Testing will be considered complete when:
● All planned test cases have been executed.
● All critical and high-priority defects are fixed and retested.
● Registration, event discovery, seat selection/locking, payment, and ticket issuance work as
specified.
● The system prevents double-booking and maintains correct seat/booking status.
● Payment success, failure, and timeout responses are handled accurately.
● Data is stored and retrieved correctly without critical errors.
● Defined performance, security, availability, and usability requirements are satisfied or formally
accepted.
● Final test results and defect status are documented and approved.

