14. Risk and Mitigation:
Risk Mitigation
Payment gateway downtime/timeout Use mock success/failure/timeout responses; verify retry
handling and release of temporary locks.
Network failure during booking/payment Handle errors gracefully and prevent incomplete or
duplicate transactions.
Double-booking of seats Test simultaneous booking attempts and verify atomic
seat locking/status updates.
Seat-lock expiry issues Verify the 10-minute temporary lock and release
behavior.
Incorrect event or seat data Validate required fields and non-negative prices/counts;
verify database consistency.
QR/PDF ticket generation failure Test generation errors and ensure the system does not
falsely confirm an incomplete booking.
Unauthorized access Verify authentication, RBAC, HTTPS, secure password
hashing, and protected functions.
High concurrent booking load Use load testing to verify the target of up to 2,000
concurrent booking requests.
Database/server failure Maintain backups and test recovery/restoration
procedures.
Limited test data Prepare varied users, events, seats, promo codes,
bookings, and payment outcomes.

